            B.q("ai-m2-3", "ai-acr", "You removed the tag v1.4 from the reminders image, yet the registry's storage use did not go down. Why, and what actually frees the space?", listOf("Untagged images are removed by the default 7-day retention policy, so the space comes back next week", "Untagging removes only the label; the image stays stored until you delete its manifest by digest", "Geo-replicas still hold the tag, so the space is freed only once replication is removed", "Layers are shared across the registry, so space is freed only by deleting the whole repository"), setOf(1), "A tag is only a label that points at a manifest, the image's table of contents, which is identified by its digest (a sha256 hash of its content). az acr repository untag removes the label and leaves the image in place. Deleting the manifest by digest, for example az acr repository delete --name larkspur --image reminders@sha256:<digest>, removes the image, and layers no other image shares are then freed.",
