            B.q("ai-m2-11", "ai-aks", "Which two statements are true? Select two.", listOf("The scheduler places the pod only on a node that still has 250m CPU and 256Mi memory not reserved by other pods", "The container can never use more than 256Mi of memory", "If the container uses more than 512Mi of memory, it is stopped and shows OOMKilled", "If the container needs more than 500m CPU, it is stopped"), setOf(0, 2), "Requests are what the scheduler reserves when it picks a node. Limits are the ceiling at run time. Going over the memory limit gets the container killed (OOMKilled, out of memory), while going over the CPU limit only slows it down, which is called throttling.",
                scenario = "Contoso Fitness sets resources on its workout-sync container in AKS: requests cpu 250m and memory 256Mi, limits cpu 500m and memory 512Mi. (250m means a quarter of one CPU core.)",
