            B.q("ai-m2-20", "ai-cosmos-vector", "Results from the new vector search are nonsense, although the query and vector policy look right. What is the most likely cause?", listOf("The stored embeddings and the question embedding came from different models", "The vector policy uses cosine, which text-embedding-3-small vectors do not support", "The vector index was not rebuilt after the API switched to the new model", "The query runs across partitions, which mixes scores from different partitions"), setOf(0), "Each embedding model places meaning in its own space, often with its own number of dimensions. Vectors are only comparable when the stored ones and the query one come from the same model, so a model change means re-embedding the stored items.",
