            B.q("ai-m2-22", "ai-cosmos-changefeed", "The team writes everything in Python and wants to react to new and changed items. Which two approaches read the change feed from Python? Select two.", listOf("An Azure Functions Cosmos DB trigger in the Python v2 programming model", "The pull model: container.query_items_change_feed, saving the continuation token yourself", "The ChangeFeedProcessorBuilder class from the azure-cosmos Python package", "A stored procedure that pushes each change to Python"), setOf(0, 1), "The change feed processor library ships in the .NET and Java SDKs, not Python. Python code either uses the Functions trigger, which runs the processor for you, or the pull model, where it reads the feed and keeps its own bookmark.",
                scenario = "Lumen Learn stores flashcards in Cosmos DB and must rebuild a card's embedding whenever the card changes. The whole back end is Python.",
