            B.q("ai-m2-23", "ai-cosmos-changefeed", "The Cosmos DB trigger uses an identity-based connection, and the function fails at start-up with a Forbidden error when it tries to create the leases container, because createLeaseContainerIfNotExists is true. What do you do?", listOf("Give the identity the Cosmos DB Built-in Data Contributor role and restart", "Set startFromBeginning to true so the trigger reads existing changes first", "Create the leases container beforehand and set createLeaseContainerIfNotExists to false", "Set leaseContainerName to the monitored container so no new container is needed"), setOf(2), "Creating a container is a control-plane (non-data) operation, which a data-plane role such as Cosmos DB Built-in Data Contributor cannot do. Learn states that with a Microsoft Entra identity, if createLeaseContainerIfNotExists is true, creating containers isn't an allowed operation and the function app isn't allowed to start. So create the lease container yourself first (for example with az cosmosdb sql container create, partition key /id) and set createLeaseContainerIfNotExists to false, which is its default. The function then only reads and writes lease documents in it.",
