            B.q("ai-m2-24", "ai-postgres", "A code review flags this line: cur.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM rides WHERE city = '{city}'\"). What should it be?", listOf("cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM rides WHERE city = %s\", (city,))", "cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM rides WHERE city = '\" + city + \"'\")", "cur.execute(f\"SELECT * FROM rides WHERE city = '{city.strip()}'\")", "cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM rides WHERE city = '%s'\" % city)"), setOf(0), "psycopg sends the parameters separately from the SQL text when you pass them as the second argument with %s placeholders, so user input can never change the statement. This stops SQL injection (input that rewrites your query).",
                scenario = "Pedalo, a bike-sharing company, has an Android app whose Python API queries Azure Database for PostgreSQL with psycopg. The city name comes straight from the app.",
