            B.q("ai-m2-46", "ai-functions", "An HTTP function calls a language model that can take six minutes, and the Android app's calls fail after about four minutes even though functionTimeout was raised. What design fixes it?", listOf("Return 202 with a status URL and hand the work to a queue-triggered function", "Set functionTimeout to -1 so the HTTP call has no time limit", "Choose the 4,096 MB instance size so the call finishes sooner", "Configure always ready instances so the call never waits for a cold start"), setOf(0), "However high functionTimeout is, an HTTP-triggered function must answer within 230 seconds because of the load balancer's idle timeout. Long work is handed to a queue, and the client polls a status endpoint (the async request-reply pattern).",
