            B.q("ai-m2-52", "ai-appconfig", "The API loads two selectors in this order: Quiz:* with no label, then Quiz:* with the label prod. Quiz:MaxTokens is 2000 with no label and 800 with prod. Which value does the production API see?", listOf("2000, because the first selector to load a key keeps its value", "800, because a later selector overrides keys loaded by an earlier one", "800, but only once the first refresh interval has passed", "An error at start-up, because two selectors return the same key"), setOf(1), "The provider applies selectors in order, and when the same key comes back from more than one selector, the later one wins. Loading shared defaults with no label first and the environment's label second is the usual way to override only what differs.",
                scenario = "Quizly's Android quiz app talks to a FastAPI backend that reads its settings from Azure App Configuration with the azure-appconfiguration-provider package.",
