            ),
            B.q("ai-m2-58", "ai-kql", "Sampling keeps only part of the telemetry. Which query estimates the real number of requests per hour?", listOf("AppRequests | summarize count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)", "AppRequests | summarize dcount(OperationId) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)", "AppRequests | take 1000 | count", "AppRequests | summarize sum(ItemCount) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)"), setOf(3), "Each record kept by sampling carries ItemCount, the number of original items it stands for (10 when one in ten is kept). Summing ItemCount estimates the true total; count() only counts the rows that were stored.",
                scenario = "Quizly keeps one trace in ten to control cost. The product manager asks how many quiz submissions the API handled each hour yesterday.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
                    0 to "count() counts the stored rows, so with sampling on it undercounts by roughly the sampling factor.",
                    1 to "Distinct operation ids still only covers the traces that sampling kept.",
                    2 to "take 1000 cuts the data to 1,000 rows before anything is counted.",
                ),
            ),
            B.q("ai-m2-59", "ai-kql", "Each console line from the worker looks like job=8812 status=done ms=431. Which query gives the average ms per status?", listOf("ContainerAppConsoleLogs_CL | parse Log_s with \"job=\" job:long \" status=\" status:string \" ms=\" ms:long | summarize avg(ms) by job", "ContainerAppConsoleLogs_CL | parse Log_s with \"job=\" job:long \" status=\" status:string \" ms=\" ms:long | summarize avg(ms) by status", "ContainerAppConsoleLogs_CL | where Log_s has \"status=\" | summarize avg(ms) by status", "ContainerAppConsoleLogs_CL | parse Log_s with \"job=\" job:long \" status=\" status:string | summarize avg(ms) by status"), setOf(1), "parse matches a pattern against a text column and turns the parts into new, typed columns, so ms becomes a number that summarize can average. extract() with a regular expression is another way to do the same.",
                scenario = "TrailMate's map tile worker on Azure Container Apps prints one line per job to stdout, which lands in Log Analytics.",
                whyWrong = mapOf(
